# knn2: MNIST kNN without OpenCV

Requires a C++17 compiler and CMake 3.15+. No OpenCV or OpenMP is needed.

Build and test:
  cmake -S . -B build
  cmake --build build
  ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure

Download MNIST with ./get_dataset.sh (requires wget and gzip), or place the
uncompressed IDX files in build/train and build/test. Run from build:
  cd build
  ./cv

Images use an owned std::vector<float>, half-size bilinear resizing with
byte rounding, and per-image min/max normalization to [0,1]. Constant images
become zero. MNIST 28x28 images become 14x14. Floating-point/rounding details
may differ slightly from OpenCV; bit-for-bit equivalence is not guaranteed.
For rectangular images the destination keeps rows and columns in their
correct order (the original OpenCV Size arguments were swapped).
The classifier, voting and k search remain the teaching implementation.
All samples participate in cross-validation, including the remainder.
Invalid k/fold values are rejected. IDX reads are checked for truncation,
and temporary pixel buffers are released automatically.
